WEBVTT

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.770
Hiroshi, hurry it up.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:40.890
What a drag...

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.350
You're going to greet
the neighbors with me.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.760
I have to say, this is a great location.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.660
Lots of greenery, and the air's clean.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.430
Hey, Mom.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.060
That house to the right of ours is kinda weird.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.010
How so?

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.920
There's only one window,
and look where it is.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.020
I took a look at the other side,
and there were no others.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.740
Come on, Hiroshi.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.600
Don't be so judgmental
about other people's houses.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.610
Guess they're not home...

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.600
<i>Yes, who is it?</i>

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.610
Hi, it's nice to meet you.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:27.360
We're the Sakaguchis,
and we just moved in next door.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.710
We just came by to say hello.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.270
I hope we can be good neighbors.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.870
This isn't much, but I hope you like it.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.710
Oh, my goodness!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.480
Ma'am, I have to ask...

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.660
Do the Numages work during the day?

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.630
I can't say.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.360
That house is always locked.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.760
But at night, you'll see a figure
in the window of the second floor,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.450
so I think someone lives there.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.730
They hardly ever go outside, though.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.540
Apparently the rumors say it's a 
middle-aged woman who lives there,

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.950
and she's supposed to be quite odd.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.540
Seems she wants to avoid
people for some reason.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.570
Huh...

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.670
And you haven't met her yet?

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:10.460
Well, I ring the buzzer,
but no one answers the door.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.160
I wonder...

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.200
Thanks for dinner.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.930
Are you done already?

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.600
Yeah, I wanna get my room
straightened up as soon as possible.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.850
Right across from the window next door...

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.910
Not sure I like that.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.710
Young man...

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.620
Young man.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.240
Young man.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.530
Good evening.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.820
Are you asleep?

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.050
How are you today?

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.090
What?

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.560
Young man...

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.910
Young man.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.540
Young man.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.540
Are you finding the new
house to your liking?

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.750
Young man...

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.310
How are you today?

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:08.000
Young man...

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.710
Come by and see me someday.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.320
I'll be waiting for you with 
the front door unlocked.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.100
What was that?

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.910
Young man...

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.900
Young man...

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.760
How are you today?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.900
Are you asleep?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.150
Let me see your face.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.920
You didn't come over today.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.610
I was waiting for you with some sweets...

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:58.100
Is it all right if I come by
and see you instead, then?

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.780
I'm on my way now.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.450
Wh-What the hell?!

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.840
Young man,

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.310
I'm going to pass you the laundry pole.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.760
Make sure to hold it tight.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.000
I'll use it to cross over.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.050
Wh-Wha...

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.560
What are you doing?!

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.600
Mom! Dad!

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.110
You gotta wake up!

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.530
What's the big deal? I don't see anyone.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.530
No laundry pole, either.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.830
I'm telling you, it happened!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.080
She was super creepy-looking!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.360
And she wanted to cross over into my room!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.040
You were probably just dreaming, Hiroshi.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.220
It really happened!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.350
Young man.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.010
Young man.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:25.310
Young man...

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.710
Are you awake?

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.740
How are you doing today?

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.450
Damn it!

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.740
Young man...

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.870
Are you asleep?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.920
Let me see your face, please.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:42.960
Just wait a bit longer.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.640
I'll be there to see you soon.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.650
Young man, it won't be long now.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.150
My hands can almost reach.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.630
I'll be there ever so soon...

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.400
It won't be long before 
I can knock on the window.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:03.160
When I do, make sure to open it for me.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:06.550
Oh, it's still too far... I can't reach.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.490
But just wait. It won't be long.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.670
I'll be there soon.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:40.980
Collection No. 067

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:40.980
<b>Window Next Door</b>

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.230
Papa died!

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.220
<i>When I was little,</i>

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.200
<i>I used to dream of my father
dying, and then I'd cry.</i>

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.810
Ah-boo!

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.720
Papa's not gonna die, Riko.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:56.980
<i>But still,</i>

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.910
<i>my anxiety about it never went away.</i>

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:04.210
<i>The one thing I fear most in the world</i>

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.800
<i>is my father's death.</i>

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:14.180
Collection No. 123

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:14.180
<b>Gentle Goodbye</b>

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:24.410
<i>A traditional wedding was part of marrying
into the prestigious Tokura family.</i>

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.630
Father, Mother,

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.680
Grandfather, Grandmother.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.030
I know I'm not much, but thank you 
for letting me join the family.

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.200
Hey, Riko-san.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.420
I guess I'll have to call you Onee-san now, huh?

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.200
R-Right.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.000
That sounds great, Tomoka-chan.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.560
<i>My husband, Makoto,</i>

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.100
<i>was willing to defy the Tokura
family in order to marry me.</i>

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.180
Cheer up, Riko.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:02.080
They'll understand eventually.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:02.680
Yeah.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.510
Oh, that's my great-grandfather
and great-grandmother.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.990
They're up in years, so they 
didn't attend the ceremony.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:14.210
Great-Granddad, Great-Grandma.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.710
this is my wife, Riko.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:19.450
It's nice to meet you.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.400
Riko...

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.000
Riko!

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:32.920
Papa!

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.130
I'm right here!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.400
Riko...

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.380
You live a happy life with
Makoto-kun, you hear me?

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.370
Papa!

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:47.810
You had that dream again, didn't you?

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.830
I'm so sorry...

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:53.310
It keeps happening.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.280
It's okay.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.490
Come on, go to sleep.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.000
Oh, honestly, Tomoka!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.310
But Mom...

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:08.340
Come on, quit laughing, Dad!

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.420
Now Grandpa and Grandma are doing it!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:17.300
<i>I have to say, this house really is huge...</i>

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:27.060
Wh-Who's there?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.180
Th... There was a gh-ghost...

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:43.820
They're not ghosts.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.190
Then who are they?

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:49.540
Come to think of it,
your great-grandparents...

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.190
I'm pretty sure the person
you thought was a ghost

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:53.750
was my great-great-grandmother...

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.370
In other words, my great-grandfather's mother.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.620
Great-great-grandmother?!

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.480
She's still alive?!

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:00.630
How old is she?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.270
She's 125.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.440
125?!

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.250
Could she really live that long?

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:09.970
I don't think you've met them yet,

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:14.660
but my great-aunt and 
great-uncle also live here.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:18.650
They're really faint and almost gone,

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:20.860
but you can still find them if you look.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.840
Almost gone?

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:26.300
My great-great grandfather and his 
mother used to be around, too,

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.370
but they've both completely vanished.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.040
What are you talking about?!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.610
Why did they vanish?!

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.990
Because they're just after-images.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.620
<i>My grandfather-in-law died the next year.</i>

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.140
It's been a while!

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.290
Yeah.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.330
Thanks for coming today, Papa.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:57.470
Riko,

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.890
is his family treating you well?

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.690
Yeah...

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.950
Thanks for coming all this way.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.120
Not at all.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.020
Well then, Makoto-san,

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:14.420
take good care of Riko for me.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.620
You can count on me, Father.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:20.820
Come on, Riko.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:24.900
The entire Tokura family is 
assembling in the living room.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.600
I guess this is the first time for you.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:34.990
My father Ryouzou's funeral
proceeded smoothly.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.860
So now, I think it's time we get started.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:39.950
Everyone,

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:43.040
think intensely about Ryouzou together,

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.540
and imagine him with all your strength.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:48.000
He may have been cremated,

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.730
but by the focused will of his family,

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:52.290
Ryouzou will appear before us,
as if he were alive!

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.670
Now, everyone, think!

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.700
Think about him strongly!

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.800
Dad!

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:07.490
Live again... Dad, Dad, Dad!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:09.810
Dad!

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.210
Grandpa didn't come back to life,

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.750
nor did he come back as a ghost.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:38.040
It's an image that was formed
by the will of our family.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.010
We call them after-images.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:44.720
They don't have an actual physical presence,

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:49.020
but they feel real to the family,

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:51.560
and it feels like we're actually talking to them.

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:55.450
But that's probably just an illusion.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:56.770
Even with conversations,

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:00.450
they never say anything that the living 
wouldn't imagine them saying.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:05.010
But we keep creating after-images
of our family anyway.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:10.520
They help fill the void left behind
when someone in the family dies.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:15.010
They go on functioning as part of the family.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.670
But over time, the image degrades.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:23.480
As time passes, they start to grow 
fainter and more transparent.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:27.800
After around 20 years, they fully disappear.

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:33.610
But those 20 years help the living let go.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:36.260
It gives them the chance
for a gentle goodbye.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:40.200
It's almost been 20 years
since my 125-year-old

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.430
great-great-grandmother
became an after-image.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:46.270
She'll probably vanish soon.

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:49.390
But at this point, neither me, 
Dad, or Grandma

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:52.500
pay her much mind anymore.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:59.210
But that's only because we had 22 years
to come to terms with it and say goodbye!

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.590
Hey, Makoto-san...

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.710
Someday, when my father dies,

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.300
would we be able to make
an after-image of him?

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:16.140
I thought you would ask that.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.600
I can see why you would want an 
after-image of your own family.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:24.230
What are you saying, Makoto?

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.290
It's out of the question!

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:31.590
What would be the point in creating
an after-image of Riko-san's father?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.420
It's just not happening.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.280
I'm sorry!

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:40.880
I was wrong to ask!

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.500
Please forgive me for making
such a selfish request!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.300
Onee-san.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.610
Don't think too badly of Mom and Dad.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.730
They're both really nice.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:05.220
I know.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.420
I was just being selfish.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:13.410
I'll go and apologize to 
them again tomorrow.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:17.490
Tomoka-chan, thanks for 
always worrying about me.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:21.200
That's because I love you, Onee-san!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:22.910
Thank you.

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:26.120
I love you too, Tomoka-chan.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:35.810
Listen... About Tomoka-chan...

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.810
I guess you noticed...

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.400
Tomoka's an after-image, too.

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:46.260
My sister died ten years ago from an illness.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:51.700
Lately, her after-image has 
started to fade a bit, as well.

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:55.150
Hey, Mom.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.310
What is it, Tomoka?

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:59.810
Don't be mad at Riko-san, okay?

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.410
She's a really good wife.

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:05.210
I understand that, but still...

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:09.620
I love you, Mom.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:13.010
I want to stay with you forever.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.550
I won't get married.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.840
That's okay, right, Mom?

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.950
Yes, of course.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:25.020
You can stay with Mommy forever.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.140
<i>The months passed,</i>

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:41.950
<i>and his great-great-grandmother,
great-aunt, and great-uncle vanished.</i>

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:46.710
<i>His great-grandparents are also
starting to look foggy now.</i>

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:50.450
<i>There was another family
funeral the other day,</i>

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:54.220
<i>and I took part in the ceremony
to call forth the after-image.</i>

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:57.910
<i>I had already done so several times,</i>

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:01.300
<i>and I tried my hardest,
as a member of the Tokura family.</i>

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:05.930
<i>But it's been eight years
since we got married,</i>

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:10.300
<i>and my in-laws are still distant toward me.</i>

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.650
<i>I thought maybe I wasn't trying hard enough,</i>

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.360
<i>so I decided to put extra
effort into winning them over.</i>

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.200
Honey! You left your lunch...

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.260
Makoto-san...

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:27.490
I thought we were meeting at the station.

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:30.190
But I wanted to see you as soon as possible!

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:40.930
That was Mori-san from your
office this morning, wasn't it?

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:44.220
You two are involved, aren't you?

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.560
Yes.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:49.700
So...

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.640
What happens now?

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.600
I mean...

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.240
I intend to marry her someday.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.500
No!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.700
I am not getting a divorce!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.030
Riko, don't worry.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:09.660
I'm not going to divorce you. 
I'll fulfill my obligation to you.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:11.020
It's my responsibility to—

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.670
What are you talking about?!

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:16.690
How are you going to marry
her without divorcing me?

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:19.950
I'm going to discuss this with her!

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:20.720
Don't!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:21.880
Let go of me!

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.070
I said stop!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.700
I-I'm sorry, Riko...

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.450
I'm sorry... that I never told you...

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:40.410
What?

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:43.290
Ten years ago...

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:46.880
It was right before we were to be married,

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:49.510
on the day before the engagement ceremony...

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.340
You were in an accident...

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:05.920
and died instantly.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.510
I begged my dad...

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:13.730
I begged him to create
an after-image of you!

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:27.820
Riko!

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.600
No...

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:33.540
It can't be...

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:41.800
<b>Ikeda 
Family
Grave</b>

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.790
If you think it's a lie,

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.020
then go to your family's house.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:41.800
There should be a marker for you 
behind the family gravestone.

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:43.930
Then...

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:45.970
I really am...

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:55.940
<i>I'm an after-image.</i>

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:59.210
<i>In ten years, I'll be gone.</i>

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:05.110
<i>Strangely, realizing that took 
a weight off my shoulders.</i>

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:07.730
<i>The next day,</i>

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:10.500
<i>I quietly left the Tokura house.</i>

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.220
Onee-san...

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:15.530
Where are you going?

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.930
<i>After apologizing profusely,</i>

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.200
<i>I bade my sister-in-law goodbye.</i>

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.160
<i>Thinking back now...</i>

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:28.680
<i>I wonder what he really thought
of a wife who would cry so often</i>

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.410
<i>after dreaming of her father's death.</i>

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:36.900
<i>Did I ever once cry because
of a dream about him dying?</i>

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:41.810
<i>I owe him an apology, too.</i>

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:45.770
<i>Ten years before I vanish...</i>

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:49.240
<b>Ikeda</b>

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:50.000
<i>I wonder, between my father and I,
who will go first?</i>

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:53.400
Riko?

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:55.710
What's wrong?

00:21:59.010 --> 00:21:59.920
Papa...

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:02.700
I'm home.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
Collection
